We perform __walk jump sampling__ with the diffusion trunk in Boltz2, a highly popular open source structure prediction model. In 
particular, by annealing at a moderately large fixed temperature, we are able to repurpose this diffusion trunk into a fast stationary sampler, 
followed by one-step denoising to produce a fast mixing ensemble of realistic proteins. On ATLAS and MDCath BoltzJump exhibits nearly 40-50%
speedup while producing ensembles of commensurate structural validity as compared to state-of-the-art structure prediction baselines.
